        "subject": "Fix digest auth uri field ignoring path parameters after semicolons"
      }
    ],
    "linked_issues": [
      {
        "id": "#6990",
        "title": "`uri` field of digest authentication incorrectly filled when the URL contains semicolons in path",
        "url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6990"
      }
    ],
    "description": "When a URL contains path parameters delimited by semicolons (e.g. `https://musicbrainz.org/ws/2/artist;name=Nirvana`), `urllib.parse.urlparse` splits the path into `.path` and `.params` attributes. `HTTPDigestAuth.build_digest_header()` was only using `.path` and `.query`, so the `uri` field in the `Authorization` header was truncated, causing authentication to fail on servers that validate the full request URI.\n\nThis was reported in #6990 with a concrete MusicBrainz API example.\n\nFix: include `p_parsed.params` when reconstructing the path in `build_digest_header()`.\n\nAdded a unit test that verifies the `uri` field includes semicolon-delimited path parameters.",
    "generated_by": "precis 0.1.0",
    "generated_at": "2026-08-09T10:00:00Z"
  },
